{
  "case_id": "2010-10-568",
  "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "John P. Elwood",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Neutral laws requiring official recusal for conflict of interest do not abridge free speech because a legislator's vote, however expressive, is not protected speech. It is, rather, a legally binding exercise of State power that he wields as an incident of public office."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Nevada Supreme Court concluded that Respondent did have a free speech right to vote, and that overrode the Nevada recusal statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you -- DO you agree with me?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ELWOOD",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELWOOD: I think you would say that it\nis not, that it is not -- voting -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Elwood, why is that extraordinary? Why aren't you willing to accept that?\nI mean, if -- if the Speaker of the House counts the votes wrong and he says the ayes have it when it's obvious that the ayes don't have it, do we review that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In July of 2009 the State Supreme Court struck it down as applied to members of the legislature."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this -- if this is accepted, it\nplaces an impossible drag on the associational rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Oh, so you're saying that the difference is that we're judges?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Did you argue associational rights below?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENKRANZ: The answer, Your Honor, is the Judiciary does not engage in political activity outside -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is no less direct than the burden that this Court recognized as unconstitutional in the Davis case, the Millionaire's Amendment Case, or in Burdick, where the only burden was that the paid petitioner would have to register to vote, which is a nominal burden, but those whose consciences were affected by a registration were kept out of the process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Elwood",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELWOOD: Now, my colleague argues that the Nevada recusal statute targets political association, and that is simply not the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-568",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4deaa1b096d72019a12d7487292effef9886088e5908b7c2cc3fd529e8e32684",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4deaa1b096d7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
